449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (The Bayes-optimal prediction at each point is a posterior majority vote. Across all possible inputs, the function formed by combining these votes need not be representable by a single hypothesis in H. Exact Bayesian averaging can also be expensive when H is very large because many posterior hypotheses must be summed. Gibbs offers a practical approximation by sampling one posterior hypothesis rather than explicitly averaging all of them. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
