<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (Including the redundant feature reduced accuracy by 0.5 percentage points and increased log-loss by 0.098289 \(about 17.81% relative to the redundant-feature model\). Thus, a violated conditional- independence assumption does not always cause a large change in classification accuracy, but it can make probabilities less reliable by counting closely related evidence more than once. Log-loss reveals this calibration/confidence problem more clearly than accuracy alone. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
