837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (first positive example it installs the literals matching all feature values. On each later positive example it removes any literal contradicted by that positive instance. Under a realizable conjunction target, all target literals remain in the current hypothesis; therefore a negative example cannot be falsely accepted. A mistake can occur only when a positive example violates an extra literal, and that mistake removes at least one extra literal. There can be at most n such removals, plus the initial positive-example mistake, giving at most n+1 mistakes. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
