/E (The PAC framework asks how many labelled examples are sufficient to guarantee low generalisation error with high probability. A mistake-bound model asks how many prediction errors an online learner can make over a sequence. PAC guarantees are useful for offline quality-model deployment planning; mistake bounds are useful when labelled inspections arrive sequentially and the learner updates after each case. Both rely on assumptions such as a realisable target for the stated guarantees; label noise can invalidate the clean bounds. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
