/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (class priors and conditional probabilities are refitted on the same training split. This reduces duplicated evidence without changing the Naive Bayes implementation or using additional model parameters. Revised workflow: \(1\) measure pairwise feature dependence on the training data; \(2\) identify exact or near-duplicate predictors; \(3\) retain one representative from each redundant group or use a dependency- aware model when the relationship is useful; \(4\) fit Naive Bayes on the reduced feature set; \(5\) evaluate log-loss and accuracy on a held-out set. A more expressive alternative is Tree-Augmented Naive Bayes \(TAN\), which permits one additional parent feature for each attribute, but it needs additional structure learning and more data. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
