931 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Q1 showed how Bayes theorem updates a rare-fault prior and how Find-S and Candidate Elimination maintain or select consistent concepts. Q2 demonstrated the MDL trade-off between model complexity and training errors, and the difference between selecting a single MAP hypothesis and averaging over the posterior. Q3 implemented Naive Bayes and showed that correlated duplicate features can harm probability quality. Q4 represented explicit dependency using a Bayesian belief network and demonstrated explaining away. Q5 used EM to estimate hidden Gaussian mixture components and selected two components by BIC. Q6 compared PAC sample bounds, VC capacity and online mistake bounds. Q7 used an observed dependency problem to motivate and test a focused redesign. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
932 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (The evidence supports a practical conclusion: the correct Bayesian or computational learning method depends on the structure of the data and the decision objective. Model assumptions, priors, smoothing, hidden variables, hypothesis-space capacity and computational cost all affect performance. A good design must be evaluated with the correct metric and its assumptions must be made explicit. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
